e/ftxui/dom/elements.hpp`/`examples/dom/gauge.cpp`, suitable for compare table/bars. Final evaluation answer: feasible; minimal design is expose loaded book text from `SearchEngine`, create a compare page that runs four algorithms on current query and loaded text, display `Algorithm / Matches / Comparisons / Time(ms)` via `Table`, use `Container::Tab({search_page, compare_page}, &tab_idx)`, switch compare to tab 1 and other modes to tab 0, and keep first version as a merged-all-loaded-books performance table.

